## Graphical abstract
Highlights
- A porphyrin (Porph: $\mathrm{C_{20}H_{14}N_{4}}$ ) scaffold is found as an emerging powerful metalloligand (ML) option. - Its combination on porous coordination polymers (PCPs) can be easily designed such as Porph-MOF or PorphCOF.
- The Porph-PCP architecture is promising as they can mimic the green nature of porphyrin with multifunctionalities.
- For the first time, we reported how PCPs can be custom-designed or functionalized based on Porph building units.   
- The current and future progress in crystal engineering of Porph-PCPs is reviewed in various respects.
